 "commander_role": {
  "value": {
   "level": "significant",
   "advances_plan": "Marchesa gives the team dethrone and returns any countered creature that dies, which makes the sacrifice engine resilient.",
   "honest_note": "The source calls the closes 'commander-native loops' (decisions L16), but none of the 48 Spellbook infinites in the list needs Marchesa: they're persist/undying loops with Thran Vigil, Metallic Mimic, Gev, Uncivil Unrest or Mikaeus plus an outlet. She's a resilience engine, not the kill. The cycle 51 M1 review (marchbr-01..11, all verified) confirms the persist-reset loops."
  },
